'''Dooku's throne room''' or '''Dooku's chambers''',<ref name="Nightsisters Guide" /> also known as '''Dooku's great hall''' or simply '''great hall''',<ref name="Dooku: Jedi Lost script">[[Dooku: Jedi Lost (script)|''Dooku: Jedi Lost'' script]]</ref> was a hall located in the main tower of [[Castle Serenno]] on the [[planet]] [[Serenno]].

==Description==
A huge chamber with a high ceiling, it contained the [[Count]]'s formal [[throne]] and desk, which were placed on a raised dais at the far end of the room. On the back of the throne stood a circular<ref name="Nightsisters" /> 22-[[meter]]-high [[glass]] [[Viewport|window]],<ref name="BMF 70" /> etched with a [[Seal of Serenno|sigil]] of [[House Serenno]],<ref name="Dooku: Jedi Lost" /> through which the sunlight bathed the room with a [[Color|greenish]] glow.<ref name="Nightsisters" /> Behind the desk, there was a secret [[turbolift]] that traveled throughout the main tower of Castle Serenno.<ref name="Spoils of War">{{TBB|Spoils of War}}</ref> The throne chamber was directly connected to the Count's [[Dooku's sleeping chamber|sleeping chamber]] by a gangway.<ref name="Nightsisters" />

==History==
===Prior to the Clone Wars===
Long before the [[Clone Wars]], [[Count]] [[Dooku]] promised [[Asajj Ventress]] to teach her the [[dark side of the Force]] however she had to prove herself first.<ref name="Nightsisters" />

===Clone Wars===
In [[20 BBY]], Count Dooku contacted [[Darth Sidious]] from the hall where he was commanded to kill Ventress. Dooku obeyed his master. Later, Ventress contacted Count Dooku there during the [[Battle of Sullust]] where she asked for his help which he denied and instead ordered a [[Recusant-class light destroyer|''Recusant''-class light destroyer]] to destroy the command ship which she crashed inside the main hanger of. He then contacted Sidious, informing him that Ventress was dead, not knowing that she survived the battle.<ref name="Nightsisters" />

Inside the great hall, Dooku fought against who he believed to be three [[Jedi]] that were actually [[Nightsisters|Nightsister]] [[assassin]]s wielding [[lightsaber]]s, Ventress, [[Karis]]. Dooku won the fight and blasted the three attackers out of the castle that led to the window inside the hall being shattered.<ref name="Nightsisters" />

[[Mother (title)|Mother]] [[Talzin]] later contacted Dooku informing him that she may have a replacement for a [[Sith assassin]] with Ventress presumed dead. Dooku was interested in the offer that Mother Talzin made<ref name="Nightsisters" /> and left for the planet [[Dathomir]] to meet with her. Later, he met [[Savage Opress]], who had been [[Magick|magically]] enhanced by the Nightsisters and took him on as his apprentice.<ref name="Monster">{{TCW|Monster}}</ref>

Later, Dooku trained Opress in the great hall, instructing him in lightsaber combat.<ref name="Witches">{{TCW|Witches of the Mist}}</ref>

